        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-31T23:18:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What happens when we add another %p extension (like %pF, for example) and something which expected it to be a pointer followed by \u0027F\u0027 is now broken? This is why I was thinking making %p on it\u0027s own being invalid was a good idea.",
